arxiv-2104-04145.description:
A 2021 arXiv research paper by Rusen Li. In this paper, we mainly show that generalized hyperharmonic number sums with reciprocal binomial coefficients can be expressed in terms of classical (alternating) Euler sums, zeta values and generalized (alternating) harmonic numbers. Keywords: generalized hyperharmonic numbers, classical Euler sums, binomial coefficients, combinatorial approach, partial fraction approach



